 # Video Use
+
+## Task constraints and exact-source cuts
+
+When a task explicitly asks for a minimal cut while preserving the source,
+those task requirements take priority over the creative defaults below. Treat
+word-level transcript times as candidate locations, not exact cut boundaries.
+Inspect the candidate and adjacent source context with `timeline_view.py`,
+then choose both boundaries independently. After rendering, inspect the actual
+output around every cut and verify its dimensions, frame rate, duration, and
+decodability with `ffprobe`.
+
+For source-preserving tasks, use the native helper with its preservation
+switches so the production renderer does not upscale, add a grade, fade audio,
+or normalize loudness:
+
+```bash
+python3 /opt/video-use/helpers/render.py <edl.json> -o <output.mp4> \
+  --preserve-source-spec --no-grade --no-audio-fades --no-loudnorm --no-subtitles
+```
+
+These options preserve the displayed source dimensions and source frame rate,
+and apply the same EDL time ranges to video and audio. Do not add captions,
+music, animation, transitions, or unrelated cuts unless the task asks for them.
+`timeline_view.py` clamps screenshot samples to timestamps containing valid
+frames; inspect the effective interval near media boundaries.
 
